   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Forms for «you» (informal) and «you» (formal or plural)",
     "texto": [
      "The imperative does not follow a single ending. Some verbs form the informal «you» with **-й/-и**: **читай**, **говори**; others use **-ь**: **открой**, **встань**. There are frequent irregular forms: **ешь** (eat) and **пей** (drink). Learn each form together with its verb.",
      "To address one person or several people politely, **-те** is added to the corresponding form: **говори → говорите**, **сделай → сделайте**. **Говорите** can also mean «you speak» in the present; context and intonation tell the imperative apart."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Requests and prohibitions",
     "texto": [
      "Add **пожалуйста** to make a polite request: **Покажите, пожалуйста, эту куртку.** (Please show me this jacket).",
      "To forbid something, **не** is used with the imperative. In general instructions the imperfective is common (**Не опаздывайте!**, «Do not be late»); to ask that a particular action not be done, the perfective is often used (**Не забудьте паспорт**, «Do not forget your passport»)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
